ThinStation Infisical Vault Appliance

This package embeds a pinned, offline-capable Infisical stack on the shared
ThinStation Docker appliance base. PostgreSQL and Redis remain private to the
Compose network and have no host port mappings.

First-run flow:
- setup-docker creates and mounts the generic persistent Docker appliance storage.
- the immutable stack seed is copied to /docker/infisical.
- /docker/infisical/setup.sh runs before Compose and creates persistent secrets.
- subsequent setup runs preserve those secrets while applying non-secret site
  overrides from ThinStation configuration.
- Compose starts Infisical, PostgreSQL, and Redis.

Supported non-secret runtime variables are documented in build/conf/90infisical-vault.
Do not put vault encryption keys or service passwords in buildtime/custom config.
